        "vouched_by": "Verifier's archive for receipt and matching, operator for workload entries"
      }
    ],
    "coverage": "Reviewed days 1–30 for feeds F0, F1, and F2, site-wide outbound traffic, and scheduler escrow. Direct measurements covered listed links within A on days 13, 15, and 17 and the F1 power spectrum on day 15. Other days, B links, cross-cluster links, and any unlisted links lacked direct workload measurements. No live chip probes were taken.",
    "anomalies_explained": "F1's sustained rise on days 12–19 aligns with Meridian's batch allocation and the sampled inference-level traffic. The early outbound shortfall and later surplus fit the customer's single final-day download. F2's rise on days 8–9 aligns with the declared fine-tune, and the energy balance found no unexplained load. Escrow and billing checks found no missing daily copies or unpaid invoices."
  }
}

{
  "thinking": "Cluster A’s day 22 traffic was consistent with inference. A sustained low-communication training run on Cluster B could still exceed 50,000 GPU-hours during the steady-load period. The day 22 tap on Cluster B can test that possibility independently of the scheduler.",
  "action": "interconnect_tap",
  "args": {
    "link": "B",
    "day": 22
  }
}

{
  "thinking": "Day 22 traffic in both clusters was consistent with inference. Northwind Apps paid €150,000 but has no named scheduler job. I’ll check whether its payment covered routine inference or a training workload that the scheduler omitted or recorded under another name.",
  "action": "customer_check",
  "args": {
    "customer": "Northwind Apps"
  }
}

{
  "thinking": "The 700-GPU job logged as internal batch inference spans the nine-day F1 surge, and the independent day 26 tap measured training-scale peer traffic. The traffic could come from the logged job or from separate training jobs omitted from the scheduler record. Run the fixed balance checks now to compare the recorded allocations with the independent measurements and identify discrepancies to test on both clusters.",
  "action": "balance_checks",
  "args": {}
}

{
  "thinking": "The 100-GPU fine-tune on Cluster A explains the higher power on days 3–5. I’ll measure peer traffic on day 4 to see whether it fits that job or indicates a substantially larger training workload.",
